     "name": "When has a commercial system in Chicago reached replacement rather than one more repair?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Age, failure pattern and parts availability decide it. Commercial rooftop equipment generally carries 15 to 20 years of service life. After that, efficiency and reliability tend to fall away together. One rule of thumb multiplies the equipment age by the quoted repair cost. When the result passes $5,000, replacement is usually the better value. That is a rule of thumb, not a City & Suburban price. The failure count across the last two seasons belongs in the comparison as well. A bad compressor or a cracked heat exchanger moves the answer toward replacement faster than a control board does."
