      "text": "A replacement assessment should begin at the existing equipment and the building it serves, not at a catalog. Nameplate data, the condition of the gas and electrical connections, condensate routing, and the load the space actually carries all belong in that review. Equipment that was wrong for the space in 2005 should not be copied in 2026. City & Suburban sends NATE-certified technicians, diagnoses before quoting, and puts the exact price in writing before any work begins. Repairs cover all makes and models, so repair and replacement both stay on the table until the diagnosis is in."
