      "text": "Where the landlord supplies the heat, the Chicago Heat Ordinance sets minimum indoor temperatures from September 15 to June 1. The floor is 68 degrees from 8:30 a.m. to 10:30 p.m., and 66 degrees overnight, under Municipal Code 13-196-410. The code lists exceptions, so it reads as the general rule. A winter change-out in a building with dwelling units therefore has to be sequenced so heat is not off beyond those minimums. In practice that means a single-day exchange, or temporary heat planned in advance. Planning the shutoff sequence first is what keeps the building inside the ordinance."
     }
    },
